const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文考察大型高频做市商跨交易场所活动时的中介与库存特征。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"The paper examines intermediation and inventory features of large high-frequency market makers operating across venues. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"研究围绕可识别做市商的跨场所交易、报价和库存资料组织，而不是仅比较普通交易量。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It is organized around identifiable market-makers' cross-venue trading, quotes, and inventory, rather than an aggregate-volume comparison. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"所需对象包括可识别交易商成交、场所级报价、库存或头寸代理、费用规则和跨场所同步时钟。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"Relevant objects include identifiable dealer trades, venue quotes, inventory or position proxies, fee rules, and synchronized cross-venue clocks. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"该论文把新型做市商放入特定市场结构中讨论；它不证明所有算法化交易者都具有相同行为或作用。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The paper situates new market makers in a particular market structure; it does not show that all algorithmic traders have the same behavior or role. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not convert association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"冻结交易场所名单、交易商分类、路由和费用制度，明确跨场所匹配规则，并记录数据是否包含暗池或内部化交易。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Freeze the venue list, dealer classification, routing and fee rules; define cross-venue matching; state whether dark-pool or internalized flow is included. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Financial Markets (2013)。缺少参与者身份、订单簿和场所级时钟时，不能将公开聚合行情解释为该论文意义上的做市活动。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Financial Markets (2013). Without participant identity, order books, and venue clocks, public aggregate prices cannot be interpreted as the paper's market-making activity. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“High Frequency Trading and the New Market Makers”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。缺少参与者身份、订单簿和场所级时钟时，不能将公开聚合行情解释为该论文意义上的做市活动。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “High Frequency Trading and the New Market Makers”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
